like-for-like: the timed encoder follows the Crystal ArithEncode step for step (static frequency table, cumulative low/high tables, 32-bit low/high update, E1/E2/E3 normalization with pending bits, final flush). The normalization loop keeps a 64-step cap where Crystal uses an unbounded `loop do`; the cap never binds. Each branch of the normalization leaves high below 2^31 before the doubling, so span = high - low + 1 exactly doubles per pass; once span exceeds 2^31 no branch can fire, and span starts at 1 or more, so the loop exits within 32 passes. Prep mode runs only the warmup rounds.
